# Enforce LF line endings for all text files, regardless of local
# core.autocrlf. Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# (the common default from the Git for Windows installer) silently
# converts every text file — including extension-less git hook scripts
# like hooks/pre-push, hooks/pre-commit, hooks/commit-msg — to CRLF on
# checkout. Those hooks are invoked via a shell (Git Bash's sh) that
# chokes on the literal \r, breaking them at push/commit time.
#
# This repo had exactly this bug once already (see CHANGELOG.md v1.8.0),
# documented as fixed via a .gitattributes file — but that file was never
# actually committed (confirmed via `git log --all -- .gitattributes`
# returning no history at all), so the bug was never really fixed.
#
# `text=auto` autodetects text vs. binary content so this is safe to
# apply repo-wide with a single rule; `eol=lf` forces LF on checkout and
# normalizes to LF on commit, for every text file, regardless of any
# contributor's local core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf